      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-14",
      "revision": 1358363208,
      "text": "Smilax australis is a vine in the family Smilacaceae, endemic to Australia. It has prickly climbing stems that are up to 8 metres long with coiled tendrils that are up to 20 cm long. The glossy leaves have 5 prominent longitudinal veins and are 5 to 15 cm long and 3 to 10 cm wide."
    },
    "es": {
      "source": "Wikipedia (es): Smilax australis",
      "source_url": "https://es.wikipedia.org/wiki/Smilax_australis",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-14",
      "revision": 133677014,
      "text": "Smilax australis es una especie de planta trepadora perteneciente a la familia Smilacaceae, es originaria de Australia."
    },
    "fr": {
      "source": "Wikipedia (fr): Smilax australis",
      "source_url": "https://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Smilax_australis",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-14",
      "revision": 210419564,
      "text": "Smilax australis est une plante grimpante monocotylédone appartenant au genre Smilax, qui fait lui-même partie de l’ordre des Liliales et de la famille des Smilacacées endémique en Australie."
    }
